{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1434894-totem-benefits-implementation-and-limits","id":1434894,"title":"Totem benefits, implementation and limits","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-02-08T18:17:34-08:00","id":1434894,"title":"Totem benefits, implementation and limits","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> I am playing with the Malta setting, as a melting pot of strangeness, and many questions arise, especially about the totems (assuming a totem with 21+ totem points):<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>How and when do the totem benefits manifest?</b><br /> AFAIK there are no restrictions in the merits that a totem can grant (besides being aligned to the totem nature), so what stops my pack from aiming for <i>Resources</i> 5 + <i>Striking Looks</i> 2 + <i>Fame</i> 3?<br /> Do all members become gorgeous rich superstars overnight? Any associated human/wolf-blooded/supernatural-creature does too?</li> <li><b>Can you get an attribute bonus twice? </b><br /> Instead of <i>+1 Wits</i>,<i> +1 Manipulation</i>, and <i>Resources</i> 2 can we get +<i>2 Wits </i>and<i> Resources</i> 2?</li> <li><b>If you do not qualify for a totem granted merit/specialty (lack the prerequisites or relevant skill) or it is contrary to your existing advantages (being granted <i>Fame</i> while already having <i>Anonymity</i>), do you get to pick a replacement of the same category (merit/specialty)?</b></li> </ol><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Thanks for the time and answers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 02-09-2021, 11:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-08T19:04:08-08:00","id":1434898,"title":"","content":"1) There are a few additional limits. Totem can't get more Totem or Dedicated Locus. Social Merits also can't be pack-members. So this cuts out recursive potential. Resources, Striking Looks and Fame are all valid if you can justify it.<br /> <br /> 2) There's nothing I can see stopping you from buying multiple bonuses to Attributes and Skills. Though the bonus can't take you higher than one more than your standard limit. So if your character already has Wits 5, +2 Wits only gets you Wits 6. So the incentive is to spread out to get the most bang for your buck.<br /> <br /> 3) The books don't seem to address this (I might have missed an answer here or on the Discord server). Personally, for prerequisites, I allow the magic of the Totem to override them (plenty of supernaturals have access to Merits that normally have other requirements for mortals). A Specialty in a Skill you have no dots in amounts to offsetting/reducing the untrained penalty. For incompatible Merits, I wouldn't allow them to have both, and give the player the option to keep their personal Merit but not be able to use it until the Totem changes or they lose it, or lose it under the Sanctity of Merits rules. I generally don't see these questions as a major issue because players are going to want a Totem that suits them in a complimentary fashion anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-08T19:13:54-08:00","id":1434900,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429937-totem-advantages-questions\">The previous thread about this. Acrozatarim is one of the writers of the original core.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> 1. That would be 10 Experiences, which would imply a very powerful totem (you would need at least 20 dots across the pack). It's doable, though. And yes, as on p92 'Whatever trait the players buy, every member of the pack <br /> gains it.' Not everyone is instantly accepted into the pack by the totem, though, so it would be a bit gradual depending on how you had the pack set up. And if you used the character creation, you would have the pack already established, so it would have been something in the past, but also likely linked to the totem somehow. An industrial totem might guide them to strike oil like the Beverly Hillbillies.<br /> 2. The writer said they suggest capping it at +1 'for sanity's sake.' But if you're okay with potentially dealing with the big numbers I say go for it.<br /> 3. They also said they believed a pre-requisite isn't necessary. Due to the supernatural endowment. But yeah if you get something contrary to what you already have you would probably be best following the replacement rule. ' If the character already has the Merit, or the maximum allowed level, choose another relevant trait of the same value.'<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-09T06:57:51-08:00","id":1434928,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the answer.<br /> <br /> Question 1 was relevant for our game because we have an established pack, with a Rank 3 totem, and Malta being Malta, a mage (my character) arrived and will be offered membership. <br /> <br /> So I join and become pretty, rich and world renowned in an instant? What justification does it have?<br /> <br /> Also my mage has Occultation 3 and Anonymity 5, which are explicitly said to be incompatible with Fame. So do I lose Occultation/Anonymity or do I get merit dots instead of Fame?<br /> <br /> The mage wants to be really low profile, but he arrived in Malta and this is currently the only pack willing to accept him so hilarity ensued.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 02-09-2021, 11:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-09T11:35:35-08:00","id":1434961,"title":"","content":"I would say that you lose the Occultation as joining the pack makes you famous since the pack is famous, is like you suddenly dating a celebrity, you are mixing up with that group you are get some attention regardless, plus it's an spiritually enforced fame, so spirit magic shenanigans are involved with your new found fame.<br /> <br /> At least that's my take on it, not sure about the circumstances of how the totem is making them famous, for all I know they are top of the list of the most wanted criminals","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","name":"Aeveth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-09T17:22:19-08:00","id":1435030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1434894-totem-benefits-implementation-and-limits?p=1434928#post1434928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I join and become pretty, rich and world renowned in an instant? What justification does it have?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, at the end of the process of joining the pack at a minimum. Joining a pack is a spiritual process even if it can be fairly quick.<br /> <br /> There's also the magical aspect of it. The Totem spirit is still a spirit, and a fairly powerful one, with things like Influence to manifest such things quickly. A Rank 3 spirit with Influence (Human Social Capital) can't create money, status, looks, or so on from nothing, but can increase such things in a target. Normally it would just be temporary, but the pack bond makes it permanent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also my mage has Occultation 3 and Anonymity 5, which are explicitly said to be incompatible with Fame. So do I lose Occultation/Anonymity or do I get merit dots instead of Fame? </div> </div> </div>There's no official concrete answer to this. The two (and a half) options that best fit the rules for you and your ST to pick from are:<br /> <br /> 1a) Gain Fame, lose Occultation 3 and Anonymity 5, but Sanctity of Merits takes effect.<br /> 1b) The same, but instead of permanently losing your Merits, they're just inactive as long as you're part of the pack and you don't trade them in for something else.<br /> 2) Keep your Merits, and get 3 dots of Merits in something else related to the Totem's theme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-09T18:43:24-08:00","id":1435035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1434894-totem-benefits-implementation-and-limits?p=1434898#post1434898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) The books don't seem to address this (I might have missed an answer here or on the Discord server). Personally, for prerequisites, I allow the magic of the Totem to override them (plenty of supernaturals have access to Merits that normally have other requirements for mortals).</div> </div> </div> </div>The example given in the book uses the Fleet of Foot merit - which requires Athletics 2. The book doesn't mention the pack members needing to have Athletics 2 to take advantage of the Totem benefit - so it seems like Totem benefits can get around the usual merit restrictions. Personally, I play this one by ear. For most merits it's fine - I'm not really sure why Fleet of Foot needs the athletics requirement to begin with - but I wouldn't let a pack take dots in Favored Form via their totem and bypass the Primal Urge requirements<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1434894-totem-benefits-implementation-and-limits?p=1434928#post1434928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I join and become pretty, rich and world renowned in an instant? What justification does it have?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not too hard to justify once you try to think about the kind of spirit that would give these benefits and how they would manifest. A spirit can't create wealth by itself, so a totem spirit that gives dots in resources might be a spirit of enterprise and industriousness. In this case, the Pack might be a corporation, and their totem spirit ensures that they always get extremely favorable deals. When a new member joins the pack they are also hired by the corporation - their new resource dots are the salary the company pays them - probably for a high position such as C suite executive - and the dots in fame are from the fact that your name will get reported in business news articles around the world &quot;lbeaumanior appointed Chief Acquisitions Officer of fortune 500 company&quot;.<br /> <br /> Striking Looks is perhaps more difficult to justify, but it doesn't always mean just pretty. It could be that the pack has a distinctive &quot;style&quot; that the totem requires new members to adopt. For the corporation example above, striking looks could be justified as new pack members simply getting tailored suits and personal stylists to make sure they're always looking their best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-02T09:32:14-07:00","id":1477904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1434894-totem-benefits-implementation-and-limits?p=1434900#post1434900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429937-totem-advantages-questions\">The previous thread about this. Acrozatarim is one of the writers of the original core.</a><br /> 3. They also said they believed a pre-requisite isn't necessary. Due to the supernatural endowment. But yeah if you get something contrary to what you already have you would probably be best following the replacement rule. ' If the character already has the Merit, or the maximum allowed level, choose another relevant trait of the same value.'</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1434894-totem-benefits-implementation-and-limits?p=1434898#post1434898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) The books don't seem to address this (I might have missed an answer here or on the Discord server). Personally, for prerequisites, I allow the magic of the Totem to override them (plenty of supernaturals have access to Merits that normally have other requirements for mortals). A Specialty in a Skill you have no dots in amounts to offsetting/reducing the untrained penalty. For incompatible Merits, I wouldn't allow them to have both, and give the player the option to keep their personal Merit but not be able to use it until the Totem changes or they lose it, or lose it under the Sanctity of Merits rules. I generally don't see these questions as a major issue because players are going to want a Totem that suits them in a complimentary fashion anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thread necromancy, but question 3 has become relevant. <b>Can Totems override splat prerequisites?</b><br /> <br /> <br /> I got inspired by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a>'s idea about making packs, and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1320203-the-pack-101-packs?p=1348517#post1348517\">used one for a new game</a>. This is supposed to be a Lust spirit, for a pack currently without Uratha, and I made the Totem Advantages<b>:</b> Persuasion +1, Seduction specialty in Persuasion, Merit: <b>Tell (Exciting)</b>, Merit: <b>Sexualized</b>, Merit: Striking Looks \u2022\u2022<br /> <br /> <b>Sexualized </b>is Ghouls only and <b>Tell</b> is Wolf-Blooded only (humans can get it but become Wolf-Blooded).<br /> <br /> We got an Uratha character and a Mage character. Can the Totem override the '<i>Ghoul</i>' part of the prerequisite for <b>Sexualized</b> for: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Wolf-Blooded members?</li> <li>Human members?</li> <li>For Mages?</li> <li>For Uratha?</li> </ol><br /> RAW, the answer should be NO to everyone, and all of them just get 2 bonus dots to use on something else since they <i>have the maximum allowed level</i> (zero) and need to <i>choose another relevant trait of the same value</i>. But mechanically <b>Sexualized</b> is just a bonus on certain rolls, nothing very Ghoulish to it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> [If it does not work, I will redesign the advantages the Totem provides].","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 04-04-2022, 12:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-02T10:43:08-07:00","id":1477910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1434894-totem-benefits-implementation-and-limits?p=1477904#post1477904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thread necromancy, but question 3 has become relevant. <b>Can Totems override splat prerequisites?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Common sense says no. You can try to adjust with a similar Merit that has analogous prerequisites, a la Beast's advice for Advanced and Epic Merits, but the Totem bond supplies benefits that mundane characters can have for a reason.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> RAW, the answer should be NO to everyone, and all of them just get 2 bonus dots to use on something else since they <i>have the maximum allowed level</i> (zero) and needto <i>choose another relevant trait of the same value</i>. But mechanically <b>Sexualized</b> is just a bonus on certain rolls, nothing very Ghoulish to it. </div> </div> </div>Given both this and the fact that the Merit explicitly attributes the bonus to supernatural qualities, it looks like this is just an attempt to maximize dice bonuses. You would do better by putting the Experiences currently applied to Sexualized and the Tell into an extra dot of Presence or Manipulation and/or the Area of Expertise Merit for the Specialty.<br /> <br /> Totems should not be able to apply benefits representing qualities belonging to a supernatural template \u2014 applying a Tell is off the table under normal circumstances for the very simple reason that <i>the Merit is contingent on their membership in the pack and the pack continuing to exist</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-02T12:50:45-07:00","id":1477919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1434894-totem-benefits-implementation-and-limits?p=1477904#post1477904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thread necromancy, but question 3 has become relevant. <b>Can Totems override splat prerequisites?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I would default to no as well. The exceptions here should be very thoroughly thought out cases. Totems are characters in their own right, not just a bunch of bonuses the players pick. A spirit that can mess with these sorts of things would need to be very connected to them by their nature. Where did a Lust-spirit get such a strong connection to vampires that it can bring out the enticing power of vitae even in those without any in them <b>and </b>such a strong connection to Wolf and Moon that it can impart Tells?<br /> <br /> It's not like the game is lacking in traits for a Lust-spirit to grant that increases the pack's ability to be sexy and seductive that don't get into these things.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-02T16:41:35-07:00","id":1477928,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the answers<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1434894-totem-benefits-implementation-and-limits?p=1477910#post1477910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given both this and the fact that the Merit explicitly attributes the bonus to supernatural qualities, <b>it looks like this is just an attempt to maximize dice bonuses</b>. You would do better by putting the Experiences currently applied to Sexualized and the Tell into an extra dot of Presence or Manipulation and/or the Area of Expertise Merit for the Specialty.<br /> <br /> Totems should not be able to apply benefits representing qualities belonging to a supernatural template \u2014 applying a Tell is off the table under normal circumstances for the very simple reason that <i>the Merit is contingent on their membership in the pack and the pack continuing to exist</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes this was the idea, maximize bonuses based on the spirit nature.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1434894-totem-benefits-implementation-and-limits?p=1477919#post1477919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would default to no as well. The exceptions here should be very thoroughly thought out cases. Totems are characters in their own right, not just a bunch of bonuses the players pick. A spirit that can mess with these sorts of things would need to be very connected to them by their nature. <b>Where did a Lust-spirit get such a strong connection to vampires that it can bring out the enticing power of vitae even in those without any in them <b>and </b>such a strong connection to Wolf and Moon that it can impart Tells</b>?<br /> <br /> It's not like the game is lacking in traits for a Lust-spirit to grant that increases the pack's ability to be sexy and seductive that don't get into these things.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea was not to imitate Vampiric connections / powers. Both merits are quite aligned to a seductive nature, but as written are very tied to the respective splats.<br /> <br /> <br /> I have updated the advantages to reflex the advice given.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 04-02-2022, 07:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,